    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72845.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "I understand. I know the magic number is 60. If you want to stop a filibuster, if you want to be able to have a cloture vote and move it on, you need 60 votes. And again, we're beating the same horse here as we talk about this. Is there a way to come up with a plan that would satisfy yourself, Mr. Chambliss, Mr. Cochrane, and Mr. McConnell, or others out of the South and not alienate yourself from the core and still come up with that magic number 60?",
