  {
    "episode_id": 72845,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72845.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Well, I hope so. And that's, that's, you know, our hope and effort and uh... you know the other thing to remember is even if we don't agree with where the bills at now all of us uh... you know desperately on the committee want to get a farm bill passed we understand how important this is uh... for our entire country And so we'll be working hard to make a session. We can reach that number. The other thing is, there's other things about this. I would like to see a very strong vote of support come out of the Senate in regard the final passage of the farm bill the reason being is it with a strong vote it makes it that much easier on our house members as they move forward again in very tough economic uh... times you're talking about spending a lot of money uh... you know i believe that this money very well spent For the most part, in the sense I'd like to see more reform in some of the other programs, but I'd like to see a strong vote so that we can encourage our House members to also have a, you know, a good vote, get something passed, and get the President's Science Bill.",
